---
import DesignLayout from '../layouts/DesignLayout.astro';
---
<DesignLayout
  section="Typography"
  title="Authority without theatre."
  focus="Can the writing feel more credible by becoming quieter, larger and easier to read?"
  description="The approved GreenSquare AI typography system using Space Grotesk for major headings, IBM Plex Sans for body and functional text, and Manrope Semibold for the logo."
>
  <section class="v3-section type-intro">
    <div class="type-opening">
      <div>
        <p class="type-label">Approved two-family system</p>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">A clear voice for consequential work.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="type-opening-copy">
        <p class="v3-lede">Space Grotesk makes the conclusion firm. IBM Plex Sans keeps the evidence clear and readable.</p>
        <p>Use contrast through typeface, weight and spacing—not military numbering, miniature labels or excessive tracking. Major headings become smaller. Body copy becomes larger. The page becomes easier to scan without becoming generic.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section type-system-section">
    <div class="type-section-head">
      <h2>One role for every voice.</h2>
      <p>The working system uses two families. IBM Plex Sans carries every functional layer so charts, tables and interfaces remain visually related to the body text.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="type-scale" aria-label="Proposed typography scale">
      <div class="type-scale-row type-scale-row--display">
        <div><strong>Page title</strong><span>Space Grotesk Semibold · 48–56px</span></div>
        <p>Decisions deserve a clear answer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-scale-row type-scale-row--section">
        <div><strong>Section title</strong><span>Space Grotesk Semibold · 32–38px</span></div>
        <p>Evidence before interpretation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-scale-row type-scale-row--subhead">
        <div><strong>Subheading</strong><span>IBM Plex Sans Semibold · 21–24px</span></div>
        <p>What the evidence supports</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-scale-row type-scale-row--body">
        <div><strong>Body</strong><span>IBM Plex Sans Regular · 18–20px</span></div>
        <p>Two specialist partners provide the strongest path to break-even while protecting the strategic accounts that carry the greatest concentration risk.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-scale-row type-scale-row--label">
        <div><strong>Data and labels</strong><span>IBM Plex Sans Medium · 14–17px</span></div>
        <p>Confirmed evidence · Owner: Maya · Due 18 August</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section type-application-section">
    <div class="type-section-head">
      <h2>Applied to an executive decision.</h2>
      <p>This specimen tests the system where it matters: a conclusion, its evidence, a quantified trade-off and an owned next action.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="type-decision" aria-label="Executive decision page typography specimen">
      <header class="type-decision-head">
        <div>
          <p class="type-label">EU operating model · FY27</p>
          <h2>Use two specialist partners. Keep strategic accounts in-house.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="type-confidence"><strong>72%</strong><span>confidence</span></div>
      </header>

      <div class="type-decision-grid">
        <section>
          <h3>Why this is the leading path</h3>
          <p>It offers €1.4m in annualised savings without transferring the accounts that present the greatest revenue-concentration risk.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>What remains uncertain</h3>
          <p>Transferred-account churn is still an assumption. The recommendation changes if churn exceeds 8% during the validation period.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="type-next-action">
          <h3>Next action</h3>
          <p>Validate transferred-account churn.</p>
          <dl><div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>Maya</dd></div><div><dt>Due</dt><dd>18 August</dd></div></dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section type-rules-section">
    <div class="type-section-head">
      <h2>The rules are intentionally narrow.</h2>
      <p>A small number of firm constraints will prevent the old language from returning through formatting.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="type-rules">
      <li><strong>Space Grotesk is reserved for H1 and H2.</strong><span>Use Semibold with restrained scale and no artificial tracking.</span></li>
      <li><strong>IBM Plex Sans carries everything functional.</strong><span>H3, body, navigation, tables, charts, captions and controls.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Sentence case is the default.</strong><span>Capitals and tracking do not manufacture hierarchy.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Body text starts at 18px.</strong><span>Long-form text is capped at 65–72 characters per line.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Manrope Semibold remains in the logo.</strong><span>Use the supplied lockup; never rebuild or substitute the wordmark.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DesignLayout>
